<http://iflastandards.info/ns/fr/frbr/frbrer/P3048> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "E.g., economics, existentialism, radioactivity, etc. A concept may be designated by more than one term, or by more than one form of the term. A bibliographic agency normally selects one of those terms as the uniform heading for purposes of consistency in naming and referencing the concept. The other terms or forms of term may be treated as variant terms for the concept."@en .
<http://iflastandards.info/ns/fr/frbr/frbrer/P3048> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://iflastandards.info/ns/fr/frbr/frbrer/C1007> .
