<http://iflastandards.info/ns/fr/frbr/frbrer/P3001> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "There may be one or more titles associated with a work. If the work has appeared under varying titles (differing in form, language, etc.), a bibliographic agency normally selects one of those titles as the basis of a \"uniform title\" for purposes of consistency in naming and referencing the work. Other titles under which the work has appeared may be treated as variant titles for the work, or in some cases as a parallel uniform title. The title of a work that forms part of a larger work may consist solely of a number or other generic designation that is dependent on the title of the larger work."@en .
<http://iflastandards.info/ns/fr/frbr/frbrer/P3001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://iflastandards.info/ns/fr/frbr/frbrer/C1001> .
